(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Chronic pain in older adults is undertreated in many community settings, partly due to) Tj
T*
(gaps in provider knowledge and systemic barriers to adequate assessment and management.) Tj
T*
(This pragmatic cluster-randomized trial tests two distinct implementation strategies to) Tj
T*
(improve pain management quality in home-based nursing services. Community-dwelling older) Tj
T*
(adults will be recruited from 22 participating ambulatory nursing agencies. Agencies are) Tj
T*
(randomly assigned to three arms: \(1\) individualized provider-level intervention providing) Tj
T*
(patient-specific pain management recommendations and support of a newly trained) Tj
T*
(specialist, \(2\) organization-level digital education platform for pain management, or \(3\)) Tj
T*
(standard care control. Primary outcomes assess changes in prescribing appropriateness and) Tj
T*
(patient-reported pain intensity. Secondary measures include documentation quality and care) Tj
T*
(process indicators. This pragmatic approach directly targets real-world implementation) Tj
T*
(barriers in ambulatory settings.) Tj
